Q: Using a prop in an import statement in Vue, using Laravel and Inertia? A: <p>ES6 imports are static—resolved at build time, not runtime. You can't use a variable in an <code>import</code> statement.</p>
<p><strong>Option 1: Dynamic import with <code>defineAsyncComponent</code></strong></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script setup lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
import { computed, defineAsyncComponent } from 'vue';
import { usePage } from '@inertiajs/vue3';

const page = usePage();

const IconComponent = defineAsyncComponent(() =&gt;
    import('lucide-vue-next').then((module) =&gt; module[page.props.races_icons])
);
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
    &lt;IconComponent /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Option 2: Icon map (better for multiple icons)</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script setup lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
import { computed, shallowRef, watch } from 'vue';
import { usePage } from '@inertiajs/vue3';
import * as icons from 'lucide-vue-next';

const page = usePage();
const iconNames = computed(() =&gt; page.props.races_icons.split(','));

const getIcon = (name: string) =&gt; icons[name as keyof typeof icons];
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
    &lt;component :is=&quot;getIcon(iconName)&quot; v-for=&quot;iconName in iconNames&quot; :key=&quot;iconName&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Option 3: Lucide's dynamic icon component (cleanest)</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>npm install lucide-vue-next
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script setup lang=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;
import { Icon } from 'lucide-vue-next';
import { usePage } from '@inertiajs/vue3';

const page = usePage();
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
    &lt;Icon :name=&quot;page.props.races_icons&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Option 2 imports all icons but only renders what you need—still tree-shakes unused render code. Option 3 is the official way if the package supports it.</p>

Q: Avoid evaluating components $slot when it&#39;s not rendered A: <p>Slots are evaluated before being passed to the component—this is how Blade works. The content runs regardless of whether it's rendered.</p>
<p><strong>Options:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Null-safe access in the slot:</strong></li>
</ol>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;x-my-component :condition=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
   {{ $arr['foo']['bar'] ?? '' }}
&lt;/x-my-component&gt;
</code></pre>
<ol start="2">
<li><strong>Move the condition outside:</strong></li>
</ol>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>@if ($condition)
    error
@else
    &lt;x-my-component&gt;
        {{ $arr['foo']['bar'] }}
    &lt;/x-my-component&gt;
@endif
</code></pre>
<ol start="3">
<li><strong>Pass a view name instead of slot:</strong></li>
</ol>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>{{-- Component --}}
@if ($condition)
    error
@else
    @include($view)
@endif

{{-- Usage --}}
&lt;x-my-component :condition=&quot;true&quot; view=&quot;partials.my-content&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>
<ol start="4">
<li><strong>Pass data + let component handle rendering:</strong></li>
</ol>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>{{-- Component --}}
@if ($condition)
    error
@else
    {{ $data['foo']['bar'] }}
@endif

{{-- Usage --}}
&lt;x-my-component :condition=&quot;false&quot; :data=&quot;$arr&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>No way to make slots lazy in Blade. The content is compiled and executed before the component receives it.</p>
